    "done_when": "The Biot harmonic kernels in nova/biot/rangefunction.py and nova/biot/elliptic.py compile as a bounded expression instead of a Python-unrolled one, with numerically identical results. Measured cause (converged-forward-solve section 2 run, 2026-10-06, fragment anchor #cfs-topology-read-kernel-scope): the traced topology read's expanded graph is 1.25 million equations and 39 MB of StableHLO at 132, 300 and 550 cells alike, so the cost is the kernel expression, not the mesh; harmonic_multiply contributes 18,533 unique equations and its contraction 9,435 of 82,248 in the point jet (value, gradient, Hessian of the coupling at a point), and harmonic_pole_moments in elliptic.py unrolls its recurrences in Python. Done when: (a) every recurrence and series in those two modules that is unrolled at trace time over a static term count becomes one lax.scan or lax.fori_loop over a fixed capacity with the term count a static operand, and the harmonic contractions are packed into batched array operations (einsum or dot_general over a term axis), so the jaxpr of the jitted point jet is bounded by the capacity and no longer by the unrolled length; (b) a new test module tests/biot/test_kernel_compile_cost.py builds the point jet (coupling value, gradient and Hessian at a point from a booked polygon or filament source, the same callable the topology read evaluates) and asserts that its jax.make_jaxpr unique-equation count fell by at least ten times against the count measured at the base revision (record both numbers), and that a cold jax.jit compile of the point jet on the H200 completes in under 30 s with the executable size in bytes recorded; (c) numerical identity: on 10,000 random evaluation points spanning near-source and far-field distances for both source kinds, every value, gradient and Hessian component agrees with the base-revision kernels to a relative error at or below 1e-13 (print the maximum), and the base-revision kernels are obtained from git show of nova/biot/elliptic.py and nova/biot/rangefunction.py at the run's recorded base revision (orientation_base_sha in the manifest, the main head at dispatch) loaded through importlib under a different module name, never by copying source into the tree; (d) negative control: a recurrence deliberately truncated by one term fails the identity test, with its printed maximum error recorded; (e) the existing biot suite under tests/biot passes by delta against the base revision on compute (one job, log committed, added failures zero, with the base failure ids listed if any); (f) an evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/converged-forward-solve/cfs-kernel-compile-cost.html with plan-evidence-for converged-forward-solve records the before and after equation counts, compile walls and executable sizes in one table, the identity maxima, the negative control and the gate command and job ids, and reckon audit-doc reports 0 errors. Gates run on compute, never on the login node: the H200 first through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs/the run directory named in the manifest/h200-kernel-compile-cost.log --wait -- tests/biot/test_kernel_compile_cost.py -vv, titan only if a real betelgeuse submission is still pending on a resource reason, and the CPU biot suite on all_debug if it has no GPU shape. Every uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync; on a compute node uv is not invoked, the shared environment's interpreter runs directly with PYTHONPATH set to the worktree. configure_dtypes() is called before any array is built and jax_enable_x64 asserted True. No public signature of either module changes; callers across nova are untouched. Commit with a conventional subject and a body; the manifest's commits line lists every commit.",
